---
// /credits — "Credits & privacy": what the site counts, and who supplies the
// data it shows (Cinemoo, TMDB — TMDB's terms ask for its sentence here). On BlogLayout's plain shell (the reading measure under a page
// header), like the 404. The footer's one small link comes here; the old
// /privacy/ 301s here (public/_redirects).
import BlogLayout from "../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";
import Body from "@whois/design-system/Body";
import Heading from "@whois/design-system/Heading";
import Anchor from "@whois/design-system/Anchor";
---

<BlogLayout
	title="Credits & privacy — Tristan Timblin"
	description="Who supplies what this site shows, and what it counts."
	kicker="Credits /"
	heading="Credits & privacy"
>
	<Fragment slot="lede">
		This site sets no cookies and has no accounts or ads.
	</Fragment>
	<div class="credits">
		<section class="credits__section" data-credits="privacy" aria-labelledby="credits-privacy">
			<Heading as="h2" size={2} id="credits-privacy">Privacy</Heading>
			<Body>
				It is hosted on Cloudflare, which serves the pages and, like any host, sees the requests
				made to it.
			</Body>
			<Body>
				Page views are counted by hosted <Anchor href="https://www.goatcounter.com" external>GoatCounter</Anchor>,
				without cookies and without storing your IP address, and only on this site's own domain:
				a preview or a local copy counts nothing. It records which page was read, the referring
				site, and the browser, screen size and country, and nothing that identifies you. The
				visitor and read counts shown on this site come from it.
			</Body>
			<Body>
				For now, Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is also cookieless, runs alongside it.
			</Body>
		</section>
		<section class="credits__section" data-credits="data" aria-labelledby="credits-data">
			<Heading as="h2" size={2} id="credits-data">Data</Heading>
			<Body data-credits="cinemoo">
				The AMC A-List card's watch history comes from <Anchor href="https://cinemoo.app" external>Cinemoo</Anchor>,
				which builds it from forwarded AMC ticket emails.
			</Body>
			<Body data-credits="tmdb">
				Its film posters come from <Anchor href="https://www.themoviedb.org" external>TMDB</Anchor> and load
				from TMDB's image servers. This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
			</Body>
		</section>
	</div>
</BlogLayout>

<style>
	.credits,
	.credits__section {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-5);
	}
	.credits {
		gap: var(--space-7);
	}
</style>
